WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.101 --> 00:00:08.307
Jack opened his eyes. He was in his living room, and it was daytime. He must have fallen asleep on the couch.

2
00:00:08.308 --> 00:00:12.253
He glanced at the clock on the TV. Oh no!

3
00:00:12.254 --> 00:00:16.463
"Mom! I'll be late for swim practice!" he called out.

4
00:00:16.464 --> 00:00:21.873
"I know." His mother walked into the room from the kitchen.

5
00:00:21.874 --> 00:00:27.855
"You must be exhausted from your early-morning heroism. I didn't want to wake you up."

6
00:00:27.856 --> 00:00:31.288
"Have you heard how Mrs. Wilson is doing?" Jack asked.

7
00:00:31.289 --> 00:00:33.914
"She's getting checked out in the hospital.

8
00:00:33.915 --> 00:00:43.929
I heard she's giving everyone a very hard time, ordering around the doctors and nurses and demanding a larger TV and softer sheets."

9
00:00:43.930 --> 00:00:47.266
"I can definitely picture that," Jack said.

10
00:00:47.267 --> 00:00:52.470
"She should be out of the hospital soon," his mother said. She smiled.

11
00:00:52.471 --> 00:00:56.324
"The poor doctors and nurses probably can't wait to get rid of her!"

12
00:00:56.325 --> 00:01:02.829
"Yeah," Jack said. "I wonder what happened though, how she ended up unconscious."

13
00:01:02.830 --> 00:01:10.560
"Maybe she bumped her head or had a problem with her heart," Mrs. Gibson said. "I have a feeling that she'll be fine."

14
00:01:10.561 --> 00:01:16.909
His mother looked closely at Jack. "You should skip practice today and get some rest."

15
00:01:16.910 --> 00:01:23.162
Jack shook his head. "I need to get to the pool. I've missed too many swim team practices already."

16
00:01:23.163 --> 00:01:33.393
Even though he couldn't compete in Saturday's meet against the Pacific Piranhas, he wanted to support his team and show Coach Shin he was responsible.

17
00:01:33.394 --> 00:01:38.884
His mother nodded. "Okay. But promise me you'll take it easy."

18
00:01:38.885 --> 00:01:45.708
By the time Jack arrived at the community pool, he was a half hour late and his teammates were already swimming.

19
00:01:45.709 --> 00:01:49.364
"It's about time you showed up, Jack!" Hulk bellowed.

20
00:01:49.365 --> 00:01:58.968
He hurled his giant body out of the water and hurried toward Jack, leaving large puddles along the way.

21
00:01:58.969 --> 00:02:07.016
"Yikes!" Jack thought, backing up. "What is Hulk so mad about? Is he going to yell at me for being late to practice?"

22
00:02:07.017 --> 00:02:14.533
The huge swimmer stood in front of Jack, his meaty face tense as he stared down.

23
00:02:14.534 --> 00:02:17.589
"You're Jack Gibson, right?" Hulk asked.

24
00:02:17.590 --> 00:02:22.422
"That's me," Jack squeaked like a baby mouse.

25
00:02:22.423 --> 00:02:30.670
Hulk lunged toward him. The movement was so sudden that this time Jack didn't have time to back away.

26
00:02:30.671 --> 00:02:34.155
"Here goes!" Jack thought as he shut his eyes.

27
00:02:34.156 --> 00:02:40.727
Getting tackled onto the hard pool deck by a gigantic brute was bound to hurt—a lot.

28
00:02:40.728 --> 00:02:44.176
He didn't want to watch his own bones breaking.

29
00:02:44.177 --> 00:02:53.343
But Hulk didn't tackle him. Instead he wrapped his giant arms around Jack's slim body and hugged him hard.

30
00:02:53.344 --> 00:03:01.740
Water dripped all over Jack. "Why in the world is he hugging me?" Jack thought.

31
00:03:01.741 --> 00:03:04.741
"Um . . . what's up?" Jack squeaked.

32
00:03:04.742 --> 00:03:12.991
"My grammy. My wonderful grandmother is alive today because of you. You saved her life."

33
00:03:12.992 --> 00:03:17.388
"Huh?" Jack said. His eyes blinked open.

34
00:03:17.389 --> 00:03:23.637
"My grandmother told me you rescued her from the bottom of the swimming pool in her new apartment building.

35
00:03:23.638 --> 00:03:32.711
I can't thank you enough," Hulk said. "She means so much to me. She taught me how to swim and coaches me and—"

36
00:03:32.712 --> 00:03:40.115
"Wait." Jack, shocked, took a step backward. "Mrs. Wilson is your grandmother?"

37
00:03:40.116 --> 00:03:44.048
"Yes. Can't you tell? I'm built just like her."

38
00:03:44.049 --> 00:03:52.017
Now that Jack thought about it, they were built alike—like a pair of King Kong monsters.

39
00:03:52.018 --> 00:04:02.831
Mrs. Wilson's bragging came rushing back to him: "My grandson, little Tommy, once swam 196 days in a row . . .

40
00:04:02.832 --> 00:04:10.837
You should see my grandson do the butterfly. Little Tommy is like beauty in motion . . ."

41
00:04:10.838 --> 00:04:19.824
Jack stared at Hulk. "Are you . . .? You can't be. You're not little Tommy, are you?" he asked.

42
00:04:19.825 --> 00:04:24.575
"I am. My real name is Thomas, but everyone calls me Hulk.

43
00:04:24.576 --> 00:04:30.994
Except my sweet grammy. She's always called me little Tommy or sugar or sweetie."

44
00:04:30.995 --> 00:04:36.563
Hulk wiped a tear from his cheek. "I don't know what I'd do without my grammy.

45
00:04:36.564 --> 00:04:43.650
She makes the best cherry pie and shows me videos of herself swimming in the Olympics and—"

46
00:04:43.651 --> 00:04:49.125
"Mrs. Wilson swam in the Olympics?" Jack asked, even more shocked.

47
00:04:49.126 --> 00:04:55.229
"Two different Olympics." Hulk, also known as little Tommy, smiled proudly.

48
00:04:55.230 --> 00:05:01.556
"One year she came in fourth in the breaststroke, missing a medal by one one-hundredth of a second."

49
00:05:01.557 --> 00:05:05.721
"Wow!" Jack exclaimed. "That's amazing!"

50
00:05:05.722 --> 00:05:12.705
Coach Shin walked over. "Hulk, get back in the pool," he said sternly.

51
00:05:12.706 --> 00:05:18.530
Then he pointed at Jack. "You skipped the first thirty minutes of practice today.

52
00:05:18.531 --> 00:05:24.210
You're already missing Saturday's meet. If you can't get here on time, you'll miss the next meet too."

53
00:05:24.211 --> 00:05:28.929
"Coach Shin and everyone else, I have an announcement," Hulk said loudly.

54
00:05:28.930 --> 00:05:33.891
"Early this morning Jack found my grandmother unconscious on the bottom of a swimming pool.

55
00:05:33.892 --> 00:05:38.861
He dived in and pulled her out. He saved her life."

56
00:05:38.862 --> 00:05:41.346
"Awesome!" a girl said.

57
00:05:41.347 --> 00:05:43.612
"Wow!" a boy said.

58
00:05:43.613 --> 00:05:48.429
"Hulk, wasn't your grandmother an Olympic swimmer?" the coach asked.

59
00:05:48.430 --> 00:05:55.920
Hulk nodded. "More importantly, she's the best grammy ever." He wiped away another tear.

60
00:05:55.921 --> 00:06:03.498
"Jack saved her life. He's a real hero. Coach, you should let him compete in Saturday's meet."

61
00:06:03.499 --> 00:06:10.330
"He deserves it," Laura chimed in quickly. "Jack lives in my apartment building. So does Hulk's grandmother.

62
00:06:10.331 --> 00:06:13.751
She's a very large woman, almost as big as Hulk.

63
00:06:13.752 --> 00:06:19.906
Jack pulled her from the bottom of the pool, swam with her to the edge, and got her out of the water.

64
00:06:19.907 --> 00:06:23.390
That shows what a strong swimmer he is."

65
00:06:23.391 --> 00:06:32.307
"Coach, I've been practicing on my own. Watch this," Jack said eagerly. He hurried to the pool and dived in.

66
00:06:32.308 --> 00:06:42.206
He swam the breaststroke with his hands cupped more carefully and his head further down, just like Mrs. Wilson, the Olympian, had told him to do.

67
00:06:42.207 --> 00:06:46.889
He zipped across the pool.

68
00:06:46.890 --> 00:06:56.449
As Jack got out of the water, Hulk and Laura and some of the other swimmers clapped and cheered for him.

69
00:06:56.450 --> 00:07:00.303
The coach nodded. "Much improved," he said.

70
00:07:00.304 --> 00:07:04.118
"Our relay team needs him on breaststroke," Hulk said.

71
00:07:04.119 --> 00:07:10.695
"And having a hero at the meet would be good publicity for the team," Laura added.

72
00:07:10.696 --> 00:07:17.614
The coach frowned. "I'm not sure the Sharks need any publicity, Laura, but I agree with you.

73
00:07:17.615 --> 00:07:24.273
Jack has shown some serious swimming skills and hard work." He nodded at Jack.

74
00:07:24.274 --> 00:07:27.361
"All right. Jack, you can swim in the meet."

75
00:07:27.362 --> 00:07:30.932
"Yes!" Jack cried. "Thank you, Coach Shin!"

76
00:07:30.933 --> 00:07:35.173
The team clapped again.

77
00:07:35.174 --> 00:07:39.251
"Let's celebrate by singing Jack's favorite song," one of the guys said.

78
00:07:39.252 --> 00:07:49.083
He started singing, "'Baby, don't you see, you're my destiny.'"

79
00:07:49.084 --> 00:07:59.571
More kids sang along. "'Listen to my pleas. You're the one for me.'"

80
00:07:59.572 --> 00:08:05.570
Jack joined in on, "'Ooh, baby, baby, baby.'"

81
00:08:05.571 --> 00:08:16.741
Soon everyone was laughing too hard to keep singing.

